35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I found that we lose a lot of time every day. Just copying things. And there are mistakes because of different records.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh dear. I found out that our ""coordination"" is basically two poor souls doing everything by hand. We're treating people like robots!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"How predictable. We have no developers available until Q3, and the customer plants have signal gaps that would make a carrier blush.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital budget is frozen. We cannot afford any high upfront costs. Furthermore, per-head licensing will create a recurring cost we cannot sustain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, the past is a mirror! The big, fancy projects that tried to do everything for everyone just died. Only the small, specific tools actually survived.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji... so maybe we shouldn't pick the most ""impressive"" one? The small things... they might help the people on the floor more.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! If we pick a project that requires ""more coordination,"" those two poor people are going to quit. We need something that reduces the load.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the budget is frozen, any proposal relying on external vendors or new licenses is a fantasy. We need something that works with what we have.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. Any proposal that scales costs linearly with the number of users is a risk to next year's budget. We must prioritize fixed-cost solutions.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with Daisuke and May! Let's find the one that solves a real, small problem without needing a huge team to keep it alive.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I just... I don't want people to keep struggling with the same mistakes every morning.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, you're so sweet. Let's make sure we don't just ""solve"" the problem by dumping the work on someone else's desk.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's stop the sentimentality. We have no developers and no signal at the plants. If a proposal requires ""real-time cloud sync"" or ""custom coding,"" it's dead on arrival.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,Logic dictates we avoid any proposal with recurring license fees or high capital requirements.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, you're always so strict! But you're right about the developers. We need something that can be set up easily!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
