60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,I think... Proposal C. It stops the misrouted deliveries and the copying of records. It helps the people who are struggling.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"Proposal D! It's a ""Workflow Assistant."" It sounds like it would save those poor people in the coordination group from writing everything by hand!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"A is a disaster. No signal at plants, no developers to build it. B is a luxury. C is a data cleanup project. D is a simple tool. I'll go with D.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Proposal A requires high capital for mobile hardware and likely per-user licenses. B is a fixed cost but doesn't solve a core inefficiency. C is a standardization effort, but D is the most lightweight.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Daisuke, C sounds good, but remember what I found? Big ""standardization"" projects usually fail because they have no owner. D is small and helpful!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,@Kenji... I see. But the people in the depot are losing an hour every day. That's... that's a lot of wasted effort.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I feel for them, but if we pick C, who manages the hub? Probably the same two people I found out are already drowning! D actually helps them breathe.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Daisuke, C is a nightmare of ""cross-unit standardization."" That's just a fancy word for ""endless meetings where nothing is decided."" D is a utility.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Proposal C would likely require a vendor license for a database or a custom build. Proposal D, as a ""shared internal tool,"" is more likely to fit within the existing software allowance.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! D is like the ""small tools"" that actually survived in the past. It's a quick win that doesn't need a miracle to work!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I guess you're right. I don't want to pick something that just becomes another meeting. I'll go with D too.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,Yay! We're all on the same page. Let's save those poor coordinators from their handwritten logs!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It's the only rational choice. It doesn't rely on a signal in a basement or a developer who's busy with accounting.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It is the only option that minimizes the risk of an unexpected renewal bill next year.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,This is great! We're actually agreeing on something! I'm so happy we're helping the team!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
